From e0491b89cfb83fd513d669bc3482c8bde190f87a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:04:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The UI kit, and the class viewer's touch layout (one code
 path)

include/arena/ui_kit.h: a screen lays itself out from a layout, the
classic one (the GBA's 30 by 20 tiles, always taken on the GBA) or a
touch one (desktop default: --ui classic|touch), whose rows are sized by
--ui-size 16|24 and which spans the screen (the safe area off while it is
open). Everything is drawn with the game's own windows, font, hand and
icons.

The class viewer reads its layout (CvLayout, ClassViewer_Layout): classic
is the screen as it was; touch has a header of buttons ([L] [R], the
filter, B Back; each presses its key), the line as a 3 by 2 grid of
24-pixel rows that take taps, the detail under it, and its own windows
for the Psynergy step. Grid movement works for any number of columns.
Three new messages (MsgArenaUiBack, MsgArenaUiPrevious, MsgArenaUiNext).

The port Makefile now rebuilds the text object when the GBA build
regenerates messages.inc.

This changes the GBA ROM (new messages, the layout reads).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ykfbWFo924wEqysLhg
